# 基础词 Unit24
# 领域: 考研
# 学科: 英语词汇
# 来源: 2023红宝书考研英语词汇-基础词
# 描述: 基础词Unit24核心词汇

{{grateful}}{/ˈɡreɪtfl/}}adj. 感激的；感谢的}}{{I am grateful for all the help you have given me.}}
{{grave}}{/ɡreɪv/}}n. 坟墓；adj. 严重的}}{{The doctor spoke with a grave expression about the patient's condition.}}
{{gravity}}{/ˈɡrævəti/}}n. 重力；严重性}}{{Gravity keeps us on the ground.}}
{{great}}{/ɡreɪt/}}adj. 伟大的；大的；极好的}}{{She is a great leader who inspires many people.}}
{{green}}{/ɡriːn/}}adj. 绿色的；n. 绿色}}{{The fields were green after the spring rain.}}
{{greet}}{/ɡriːt/}}v. 问候；迎接}}{{She greeted her guests at the door with a warm smile.}}
{{ground}}{/ɡraʊnd/}}n. 地面；根据}}{{The ball fell to the ground and rolled away.}}
{{group}}{/ɡruːp/}}n. 组；群；v. 分组}}{{The students were divided into groups for the project.}}
{{grow}}{/ɡrəʊ/}}v. 生长；增长；种植}}{{The city's population has grown rapidly in recent years.}}
{{guarantee}}{/ˌɡærənˈtiː/}}n. 保证；v. 保证}}{{The product comes with a two-year guarantee.}}
{{guard}}{/ɡɑːrd/}}n. 守卫；v. 保护}}{{The security guard watches the building at night.}}
{{guess}}{/ɡes/}}v. 猜测；n. 猜测}}{{Can you guess how many students are in the class?}}
{{guest}}{/ɡest/}}n. 客人；宾客}}{{The hotel welcomes guests from all over the world.}}
{{guide}}{/ɡaɪd/}}n. 导游；指南；v. 引导}}{{The tour guide explained the history of the ancient temple.}}
{{guilty}}{/ˈɡɪlti/}}adj. 有罪的；内疚的}}{{He was found guilty of the crime and sentenced to prison.}}
{{gun}}{/ɡʌn/}}n. 枪；炮}}{{The police officer carried a gun for protection.}}
{{guy}}{/ɡaɪ/}}n. 家伙；人}}{{He is a nice guy who helps everyone around him.}}
{{habit}}{/ˈhæbɪt/}}n. 习惯；习性}}{{Reading before bed is a good habit to develop.}}
{{hair}}{/heər/}}n. 头发；毛发}}{{She has long black hair that reaches her shoulders.}}
{{half}}{/hɑːf/}}n./adj. 一半（的）}}{{Half of the students passed the entrance exam.}}
{{hall}}{/hɔːl/}}n. 大厅；走廊}}{{The concert will be held in the main hall of the university.}}
{{hand}}{/hænd/}}n. 手；v. 递}}{{She handed me the report with a smile.}}
{{handle}}{/ˈhændl/}}v. 处理；n. 把手}}{{The manager handles all customer complaints personally.}}
{{hang}}{/hæŋ/}}v. 悬挂；绞死}}{{She hung the painting on the wall above the fireplace.}}
{{happen}}{/ˈhæpən/}}v. 发生；碰巧}}{{What happened while I was away?}}
{{happy}}{/ˈhæpi/}}adj. 快乐的；幸福的}}{{She felt happy when she received the good news.}}
{{harbor}}{/ˈhɑːrbər/}}n. 港口；v. 怀有（想法等）}}{{The ship arrived at the harbor early in the morning.}}
{{hard}}{/hɑːrd/}}adj. 困难的；硬的；adv. 努力地}}{{She worked hard to achieve her goals.}}
{{hardly}}{/ˈhɑːrdli/}}adv. 几乎不；刚刚}}{{I could hardly hear what he was saying.}}
{{harm}}{/hɑːrm/}}n./v. 伤害；损害}}{{Smoking does great harm to your health.}}
{{harmony}}{/ˈhɑːrməni/}}n. 和谐；协调}}{{The community lives in harmony with nature.}}
{{harvest}}{/ˈhɑːrvɪst/}}n. 收获；v. 收割}}{{The farmers celebrated a good harvest this year.}}
{{haste}}{/heɪst/}}n. 匆忙；急忙}}{{In her haste to leave, she forgot her phone.}}
{{hate}}{/heɪt/}}v. 憎恨；n. 憎恨}}{{I hate waiting in long lines.}}
{{have}}{/hæv/}}v. 有；吃；经历}}{{I have a meeting at 10 o'clock this morning.}}
{{head}}{/hed/}}n. 头；领导；v. 前往}}{{She is the head of the marketing department.}}
{{headline}}{/ˈhedlaɪn/}}n. 标题；头条新闻}}{{The story made headlines around the world.}}
{{headquarters}}{/ˌhedˈkwɔːrtərz/}}n. 总部；司令部}}{{The company's headquarters are located in San Francisco.}}
{{health}}{/helθ/}}n. 健康；卫生}}{{Good health is more valuable than wealth.}}
{{hear}}{/hɪər/}}v. 听见；听说}}{{I heard a strange noise coming from the basement.}}
